course: dictionary
lesson: 9233
title: Words for music makers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A songwriter is a person who writes songs. They might write the words, the tune, or both. You can often work out a word like this from the sentence around it.
explain: The words of a song are its lyrics, and the tune is its melody. «Some songwriters start with words, some with a tune or chords, some with a beat; there is no single correct way.» So a songwriter can begin in many different places.
explain: A singer-songwriter writes and sings their own songs. A cover is a new performance of someone else's song. «A cover is a new performance of someone else's song; covers are normal, and when they are released, the songwriters are named and paid.»
fact: A songwriter is a person who writes songs.
fact: Lyrics are the words of a song, and melody is its tune.
fact: «Streaming means playing music over the internet without owning a copy.»
fact: Streaming apps are reported to pay only a fraction of a penny per play, shared between the record label, the songwriters and the artist.
fact: A singer-songwriter writes and sings their own songs.
exercise: What is a songwriter? | *A person who writes songs: the words, the tune, or both | A person who sells records in a shop | A person who only dances on stage | A person who reads the news on the radio
exercise: In a song, what are the lyrics? | A picture on the front of the record | *The words of the song | The name of the record company | The tune of the song
exercise: What is a singer-songwriter? | A singer who never writes anything | *Someone who writes and sings their own songs | A person who takes photos at concerts | Someone who only writes books
test: «A cover is a new performance of someone else's song.» What is a cover? | A song with no tune | A song written by the singer who first recorded it | *A new performance of someone else's song | A type of concert ticket
test: The text says going to shows or buying music straight from the artist can help them far more than streaming. Which is true? | *Going to shows or buying straight from the artist can help them far more | Songwriters never get paid | Streaming always pays a whole pound for each play | Only the singer ever earns money from a song
exam: «Streaming means playing music over the internet without owning a copy.» What does streaming mean? | Singing in a choir | *Playing music over the internet without owning a copy | Writing lyrics on paper | Buying a copy of a record to keep
